    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are leaning into stolen base upside today, positioning **Nasim Nunez** (62.09) as our primary engine against the volatile arm of Feltner. Despite hitting ninth, **Nasim Nunez** secures the highest efficiency score of the day because his elite sprint speed profile thrives against a high-xERA starter (5.10), providing a significant floor in the SB category. **Sam Antonacci** (59.34) is our second-most vital start, anchored by his optimal leadoff position against Rocker. While the matchup against Rocker is league-average, **Sam Antonacci**\u2019s plate discipline and speed-first profile against a 4.36 xERA arm make him a strong play to set the table for the heart of the order.\n\nIn the middle of the lineup, **Tommy White** (55.05) and **Miguel Vargas** (54.64) are solid starts, though both face moderate resistance. **Tommy White** benefits from a positive park factor that helps offset the neutral platoon disadvantage against Matthews, while **Miguel Vargas** holds his value by slotting into the #3 hole, despite a dip in dynamic platoon efficiency. **Jackson Merrill** (51.55) rounds out the active roster; his score is suppressed by a difficult matchup against Ashcraft, whose 3.28 xERA represents our toughest hurdle today. We are monitoring the status of **Jordan Westburg** and **Heliot Ramos**, who were the closest to cracking the lineup but ultimately sat due to tighter platoon margins. With our core stars like **Kyle Tucker**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Gunnar Henderson** enjoying a scheduled day off, we are relying on this speed-centric configuration to manufacture runs. We will keep a close watch on weather reports, but as of now, the primary risk remains the high-end talent of the opposing starters like Ashcraft, which could squeeze our AVG category.",
